{"kind":"assert","text":"C2 (208a0378): the list owed before code, on ruling b1b1d492 and carry 556eca2b, read at main 324a0679. Paths are under packages/derive/src unless named.\n\n1. Readers of `Own` (fields.ts:28). packages/client/src reads none.\n- Absence reads as \"nothing\", with no fault: `equal` operand.ts:665 and guard-value.ts:44; `entryOf` operand.ts:468,474; effects.ts:86-88; `openerOf` outcomes.ts:260; sends.ts:130.\n- Refuses or answers `unavailable`: operand.ts:372-376; guard-value.ts:124; sends.ts:120,150; send-value.ts:19; prepare.ts:231; device-command.ts:21,71,83; hold.ts:817; `judgeFloor` floor.ts:169-173.\n- Throws: `preparationStatus` prepare.ts:322; settle.ts:235 (RuleFault); fold.ts:305 (FoldError).\n- Skips work with no trace: `priorDetachedBounds` handlers.ts:136-139; gitread.ts:72; floor.ts:52,67,129,142,191.\n- Passes Own on: fold.ts:106-111, draws.ts:91, floor.ts:50-57; `givenTo` marks.ts:502 and genesis.ts:202 give a null Own.\n- Platform rules read `RuleGiven.own` inside `run`: destination.ts, the rules-certificate versions, destination-evidence(-funding)-v17.ts, evidence-bound-fence-v17.ts, publication-standing.ts, register.ts:252, application-install.ts:126,265, application-install-creation.ts:63,65, repository-binding-cohort-data.ts:21,27, versions.ts:43,49.\n- Builders: scope core.ts:61 `ownOf` and turn.ts:43; replay floor.ts:7 `floorOwn`; define story.ts:112. The fold reads Own only through `decisionBinding` (draws.ts:91), `itemSettlementBinding` (fold.ts:104) and a `floor` entry.\n\n2. `context.retained`: the port is settle.ts:116, and settle.ts:239 is its one reader, through `settleOutcome`. Neither `judgeAct` nor `applyEntry` reaches it. `Own.retained` (fields.ts:32) is read at floor.ts:125.\n\n3. `fixedHash`: the port is state.ts:232, with `MemoryState` at state.ts:412. fold.ts:301-314 reads it through `fixedRowsOf` and `rekeyFixed`. A replica that folds from genesis holds every hash, and only a floor nulls one. C2 needs no `Unheld` here; SS2 does.\n\n4. `RetainedOwn` (fields.ts:46): `retainedRow` is read at retained-use.ts:155 and `retainedBirth` at retained-use.ts:236. Only `readRetainedUses` reads them, and its one caller is scope core.ts:111 `retainedUsesOf`. No judge and no fold reads either port.\n\n5. Catch sites on a path to Own:\n- `run` marks.ts:546-552 turns any throw into RuleFault.\n- `unjudged` marks.ts:475-482 turns RuleFault into `unavailable` and passes other throws on. It wraps judge.ts:185,191,207, genesis.ts:114,120, delivery.ts:125,131 and settle.ts:71,151,166,172. An `Unheld` that a derive reader throws directly (for example operand.ts:375) leaves `judgeAct` as a throw.\n- `readRetainedUses` retained-use.ts:130-270 turns any throw into `invalid-use` or `invalid-origin`. It is on no judge or fold path.\n- 16 catch sites in packages/platform turn a throw inside `run` into null, false or `unavailable()`, before `run` sees it. Only the record catches these.\n- No other derive catch wraps a read of Own: fold.ts:90 and draws.ts:184 catch StandingError, and ancestry.ts:257 catches Stop. `applyEntry` has no catch.\n\n6. Tests. The replica's Own runs over a generated journal with position k removed.\n- `run`/`unjudged`: a `gateRules` guard (test/fixtures-marks.ts:59) that reads given.own(k). `judgeAct` answers `unavailable`, and the prediction reads `not-judged`.\n- Direct throw: an act whose local fact field names k. `judgeAct` throws, and the prediction reads `not-judged`.\n- Platform catch: a guard that wraps given.own(k) in try/catch and returns null. `judgeAct` answers, and the prediction reads `not-judged`.\n- Fold: `applyEntry` with an Own that lacks k. The replica stops.\nThe replica builds its Own in packages/client on the pattern of `floorOwn`. A shared form would need a new derive export, and 208a0378 says to ask first.\n\nQuestions for a ruling, each with a proposal:\na. One test per platform catch site (16), or one representative `gateRules` test? Proposal: one representative test.\nb. The replica can give a plain `Own`, not `RetainedOwn`, because no judge or fold reads the retained ports. Proposal: C2 implements neither port and drops the `readRetainedUses` test.\nc. When the replica is `behind`, does `Own(seq)` above its head answer null or throw `Unheld`? Proposal: null, because the prediction states its head.\nd. derive already exports a type `Unheld` (grant.ts:212, a grant failure name). Proposal: the client's fault is named `UnheldEntry`.\ne. When `judgeAct` throws and the record is empty, the throw is the judge's own failure. Proposal: the client throws it on.\nf. A replica that folds from genesis keeps every entry, so in C2 `Unheld` fires only through a test seam in the replica's entry store. Proposal: add that seam, internal to packages/client."}